libdiginet (0.1.4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * 0.1.4: the changelog carries #48, the Control|24 session rule and RENEWED
  * ksy: V-Pot, jog and section-key frames from a Control|24
  * docs, fuzz: the blank a new desk session makes and RENEWED in
    protocol.md, 193 records, the transport floor at 441
  * fuzz: RENEWED is no way into ONLINE, and the seed e1-after-failed-wake
    keeps the case the fuzzer found
  * fuzz: the latest sabotage on its line
  * fuzz: the sabotage headers on their lines, a record holds the RENEWED
    notice
  * transport: a Control|24's first e1 in a session it opened on our e2 is
    ONLINE again (RENEWED)
  * docs, fuzz: the Control|24 session rule as the captures show it, 192
    records, the transport floor at 435
  * ksy: read real Control|24 frames, and name what they show
  * fuzz: the sabotage headers name the lines of their checks
  * fuzz: the e0 records on the checks they reach, diginet_codec.h references
    on their lines
  * fuzz: the records, seeds and sabotage patches follow the Control|24 a0
    rule
  * transport: a Control|24 is online on the a0 again, and its e0 before an
    e1 gets an e2
  * docs, fuzz: the held session across a host restart in protocol.md, 191
    records
  * fuzz: the latest sabotage names its line
  * fuzz: the records and sabotage headers name their lines, and a record
    holds the e1 proof set after the wake
  * transport: the e1 that wakes a session is its proof, so a restarted host
    is online on the a0
  * 0.1.4: a desk that stops ACKing ends its session again
  * docs, fuzz: the vanished desk in protocol.md, the counts and the
    transport floor at 426
  * fuzz: the ACK-loss record on the state check it reaches, the latest
    sabotage on its line
  * fuzz: the records name the lines they break, and two records hold the
    restored ACK loss
  * transport: a host frame unACKed through every retry ends the session
    again (#45)

